{
  "text": " This tactic is about as close as it gets. I once ran all my emails and web pages through this process and got a permanent 50% boost. So here's how it works. Run every script you write, every webinar, every email through a reading level calculator. It'll tell you the grade. Then keep correcting it until it's below third grade. I use Hemingway app. You can use whatever one you want. It's free and I have no affiliation. What does below third grade actually mean? It really just means simpler words, shorter sentences, fewer adverbs, no passive language, no excess words. If you want to take this to the next level, actually write inside of Hemingway. This gives you real-time feedback and makes you a better writer that much faster. It was one of the things that absolutely transformed my writing. I really can't emphasize this enough. I strongly recommend writing inside of the app because it will give you such good real-time feedback. I'm repeating this on purpose because I think it's such a big deal. To be clear, simplifying language doesn't mean you attract dumb people. It means you make it easier for higher level people.",
